# Ghost Platform Backup Restore Guide

## Backup Locations

- PostgreSQL: `{{ ghost_backup_dir }}/postgres/`
- Redis: `{{ ghost_backup_dir }}/redis/`
- Full System: `{{ ghost_backup_dir }}/`
{% if backup_s3_bucket is defined %}
- S3 Bucket: `s3://{{ backup_s3_bucket }}/ghost-backups/{{ inventory_hostname }}/`
{% endif %}

## Restore PostgreSQL Database

```bash
# Stop the application
cd {{ ghost_install_dir }}
docker compose stop ghost-webapi

# Restore from backup
gunzip -c {{ ghost_backup_dir }}/postgres/latest.sql.gz | \
  docker exec -i ghost-postgres psql -U ghost

# Restart application
docker compose start ghost-webapi
```

## Restore Redis Data

```bash
# Stop Redis
docker compose stop redis

# Extract backup
gunzip -c {{ ghost_backup_dir }}/redis/latest.rdb.gz > /tmp/dump.rdb

# Copy to Redis volume
docker cp /tmp/dump.rdb ghost-redis:/data/dump.rdb

# Start Redis
docker compose start redis
```

## Restore Full System

```bash
# Stop all services
cd {{ ghost_install_dir }}
docker compose down

# Extract full backup
tar -xzf {{ ghost_backup_dir }}/latest-full.tar.gz -C {{ ghost_install_dir }}

# Start all services
docker compose up -d
```

{% if backup_s3_bucket is defined %}
## Restore from S3

```bash
# Download latest backup from S3
aws s3 cp s3://{{ backup_s3_bucket }}/ghost-backups/{{ inventory_hostname }}/ \
  {{ ghost_backup_dir }}/ --recursive

# Then follow restore procedures above
```
{% endif %}

## Verify Restore

```bash
# Check database connectivity
docker exec ghost-postgres psql -U ghost -c "SELECT version();"

# Check Redis
docker exec ghost-redis redis-cli ping

# Check application health
curl http://localhost:8080/health
```

